---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo for Shopify Marketing';
const description = 'A focused ActiveCampaign vs Klaviyo comparison for Shopify data, automation, CRM context, pricing, and operating fit.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} datePublished="2026-07-23">
  <article class="py-12 md:py-20"><div class="container max-w-4xl">
    <a href="/compare" class="text-sm text-muted inline-block mb-6">← All comparisons</a>
    <header class="mb-10"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary mb-3">Two-product Shopify comparison</p><h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">{title}</h1><p class="text-xl text-muted">ActiveCampaign and Klaviyo can both support Shopify lifecycle marketing, but one centers CRM and sales context while the other centers commerce data and merchandising. This page compares only those two products.</p></header>
    <section class="rounded-xl border border-primary/20 p-6 mb-10"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Short answer</h2><p>Choose ActiveCampaign when Shopify activity must sit beside lead scoring, deal stages, sales ownership, or broader CRM automation. Choose Klaviyo when product catalog, browse, cart, purchase, and customer-value data should drive ecommerce segments and flows.</p><p class="mt-3">Do not compare only template counts or headline pricing. Model profiles or contacts, events, SMS, seats, integrations, attribution, consent, suppression, and the operator time required to keep product and customer data accurate.</p></section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Decision snapshot</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10"><table><thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>ActiveCampaign</th><th>Klaviyo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Best fit</td><td>Shopify plus CRM and sales automation</td><td>Commerce-led lifecycle and merchandising</td></tr><tr><td>Core strength</td><td>Deals, lead scoring, ownership, and conditional automation</td><td>Catalog, customer events, segments, and ecommerce reporting</td></tr><tr><td>Main trade-off</td><td>More configuration for a pure DTC operation</td><td>Profile, channel, and data governance costs can grow quickly</td></tr><tr><td>Pricing question</td><td>How do contacts, seats, CRM, and feature tiers scale?</td><td>How do profiles, messages, channels, and attribution scale?</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">ActiveCampaign: when it fits</h2><p>ActiveCampaign is a strong candidate when a Shopify business has more than a marketing queue: wholesale or sales-assisted accounts, deal stages, lead scoring, or customer ownership that must influence follow-up. It can connect commerce activity to a broader revenue process when the team is prepared to define which system owns each field.</p><p class="mt-3">For a DTC pilot, keep the scope narrow. Test product, order, refund, consent, and purchase suppression; then verify that a sales or support handoff removes the customer from promotional automation. Compare the full contact-and-seat cost at the next realistic volume, not just the entry plan.</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Klaviyo: when it fits</h2><p>Klaviyo is the more natural choice when the store’s most valuable signals are catalog views, product affinity, cart state, order history, predicted value, and repeat-purchase timing. It earns its complexity when the merchandising team can act on those segments and maintain a reliable event and product feed.</p><p class="mt-3">Pilot one welcome, cart, or post-purchase flow with explicit recent-purchase and refund suppression. Validate profile merges, catalog updates, consent, attribution windows, SMS permissions, and the next profile threshold before expanding to every collection or channel.</p>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Controlled Shopify pilot</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>ActiveCampaign</th><th>Klaviyo</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Identity</td><td>Contact, account, deal, and Shopify customer relationship</td><td>Profile, customer, catalog, and order relationship</td></tr><tr><td>Trigger</td><td>Shopify event, score change, deal stage, or owner action</td><td>Browse, cart, product, order, or value event</td></tr><tr><td>Suppression</td><td>Purchase, refund, consent, deal, and support state</td><td>Purchase, refund, consent, frequency, and channel state</td></tr><tr><td>Outcome</td><td>Qualified revenue, repeat purchase, or sales handoff</td><td>Incremental purchase, repeat value, margin, or retained customer</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Final verdict</h2><p>ActiveCampaign wins when CRM ownership and Shopify marketing need to operate together. Klaviyo wins when commerce data depth and merchandising execution are the center of gravity. Choose after a representative pilot proves identity, event freshness, suppression, reporting, and twelve-month operating cost.</p><p class="mt-6">Continue with the <a href="/blog">email-marketing guides</a>, <a href="/for/high-aov">high-AOV store guidance</a>, and <a href="/alternatives">alternatives library</a>.</p>
  </div></article>
</BaseLayout>
